{
  "reasoning": "For LionMatch to drive adoption among Columbia undergraduates, it must solve a real friction point better than existing alternatives — so we need to know where students currently struggle most (discovery, matching quality, application support, or follow-through), which opportunity types they prioritize, and what would make them choose LionMatch over LinkedIn, Handshake, or word-of-mouth. We also need to surface any unmet needs we haven't anticipated, which is why one open question is essential.",
  "title": "LionMatch: What Should We Build Next?",
  "questions": [
    {
      "text": "Which types of opportunities are you actively looking for right now? (Select all that apply)",
      "type": "multi",
      "options": ["Internships", "Research positions", "Student clubs / organizations", "Fellowships & scholarships", "Part-time or on-campus jobs", "Volunteer / community engagement", "I'm not actively looking right now"]
    },
    {
      "text": "How do you currently find most of your opportunities at Columbia?",
      "type": "single",
      "options": ["Handshake", "LinkedIn", "Word of mouth / friends", "Columbia department or advisor emails", "Club listservs or GroupMe", "LionMatch", "General web search", "Other"]
    },
    {
      "text": "What is the biggest frustration you have when searching for opportunities at Columbia?",
      "type": "single",
      "options": ["Too many irrelevant results — hard to filter", "Don't know where to start or what I qualify for", "Opportunities I find are already closed or outdated", "Hard to get responses after applying", "Lack of peer reviews or insider info about opportunities", "No single place that covers all opportunity types", "I don't have a major frustration"]
    },
    {
      "text": "How useful would each of the following LionMatch features be to you? (1 = Not useful at all, 5 = Extremely useful)",
      "type": "scale",
      "options": ["Personalized opportunity recommendations based on my major and interests", "Peer reviews and ratings of internships, labs, and clubs", "Deadline reminders and application tracking", "Direct messaging with current members or past interns", "AI-generated cover letter or application drafts", "A unified dashboard for internships, research, clubs, and fellowships"]
    },
    {
      "text": "If LionMatch recommended an opportunity to you, how important are each of the following for you to trust and act on that recommendation? (1 = Not important, 5 = Very important)",
      "type": "scale",
      "options": ["It matches my stated major or career interest", "Other Columbia students have reviewed it positively", "The deadline is upcoming and I have time to apply", "A friend or classmate has done it before", "The organization or lab is well-known"]
    },
    {
      "text": "What would most likely make you choose LionMatch over Handshake or LinkedIn for finding opportunities?",
      "type": "single",
      "options": ["It's Columbia-specific — more relevant results", "Better personalization to my profile", "Peer reviews and honest insider info", "Easier application process or tracking", "It covers all opportunity types in one place", "I wouldn't — I prefer existing tools"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Is there anything about finding opportunities at Columbia that frustrates you or that you wish a tool like LionMatch would solve — that we haven't asked about?",
      "type": "open",
      "options": []
    }
  ],
  "success_looks_like": "A clear winner emerges among the feature ratings (Q4) that aligns with the top-cited frustration (Q3) and the stated reason to switch (Q6), with the open responses (Q7) either confirming that pattern or surfacing a consistent unmet need not covered by the closed questions."
}
